course: dictionary
lesson: 16131
title: Whiten: making things white or pale
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Whiten is a verb, a doing word. It shows an action: making something whiter, or becoming white or pale. «Mum whitened the old sink with bleach.» The sink was not very white before, and the bleach made it whiter.
explain: Look at the ending. Whiten, whitens, whitened and whitening all come from the same root, white, with -en added. The -en often means "to make" or "to become", like brighten, soften and lighten. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Her knuckles whitened as she gripped the rope.» Does "became pale" make sense here? Yes, it does.
explain: Context can show a second meaning. «Her face whitened when she heard the crash.» Nobody painted her face. She went pale because she was frightened. So whiten can mean to become white or pale, for example from fear or cold.
fact: Whiten means to make something whiter or paler.
fact: Whiten also means to become white or pale, for example from fear or cold.
fact: Whiten is a verb: whiten, whitens, whitened, whitening.
fact: «Whiten teeth» means to make teeth whiter, which is what toothpaste claims to do.
fact: «Whitened with fear» means pale because you are frightened.
exercise: «The toothpaste promises to whiten your teeth.» What does whiten mean here? | To break teeth | *To make teeth whiter | To hide teeth behind your lips | To make teeth smaller
exercise: «Her knuckles whitened as she gripped the rope.» What is happening to her knuckles? | They are turning green | They are growing bigger | *They are becoming pale | They are being washed
exercise: Which word is a form of the verb whiten? | whiteboard | whitest | *whitens | whiteness
test: «The bleach will whiten the stained shirt.» What will happen to the shirt? | It will become darker | It will be torn | *It will become whiter | It will shrink
test: Which sentence uses whiten to mean become pale from fear? | «She made a sandwich for lunch.» | «The rain fell all day.» | «The cat ran up the tree.» | *«His face whitened when the lights went out.»
exam: «The cold wind whitened her cheeks.» What does whiten mean here? | Painted her cheeks | Made her cheeks bigger | *Made her cheeks pale | Made her cheeks warm
